{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-tm-worked-examples-table2-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:tm-worked-examples-table2-data","kind":"table","title":"Table 2 from tm-worked-examples","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tm-worked-examples"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"tm-worked-examples-table2-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"tbl:tm-worked-examples-table2-data\"></a><p>Each row records a crossing by its endpoint pair, its crossing type, and the associated transfer matrix. Here the single <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(1, 2)</code> crossing between proton <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{p}_1</code> and neutron <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{n}_2</code> is of mixed type, and so contributes the mixed transfer matrix <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{\\mathrm{mix}}</code>.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Crossing</th>\n<th>Pair</th>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Transfer matrix</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(1, 2)</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{p}_1</code>-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{n}_2</code></td>\n<td>mix</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{\\mathrm{mix}}</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-transfer-matrices/tm-worked-examples-table2-data.md","heading":"Table"}
